{{$NEXT}}

 - Async requests no longer follow redirects (max_redirects => 0), matching
   WWW::Crawl4AI: a 3xx fails as an api error carrying the 3xx status_code
 - health resolves 0 and never fails a Future; on a failed check (transport
   error, or any non-2xx answer, a 3xx included) it warns once, on one line,
   "crawl4ai health check failed: <reason>", like WWW::Crawl4AI::Client
 - The timeout attribute is now applied to every async request (passed to
   Net::Async::HTTP do_request); a stalled request fails as a transport error and
   is retried, so a hung Crawl4AI no longer leaves the Future pending forever
 - cpanfile: declare URI (runtime) and Moo (test)
 - crawl / markdown Result now surfaces response_headers from the async path,
   mirroring the sync WWW::Crawl4AI facade (regression test t/55-response-headers.t)
 - Require WWW::Crawl4AI 0.007 (up from 0.002) for response_headers support
   and the dying health parser behind the health warning

0.001     2026-05-30 01:01:52Z

 - Initial release
 - IO::Async / Net::Async::HTTP client wrapping WWW::Crawl4AI
 - Future-returning low-level endpoints: crawl_once, md, job_submit, job_status, health
 - Async, orchestrated strategy chain: markdown / crawl return Future<WWW::Crawl4AI::Result>
 - crawl_job_and_wait flow helper: submit /crawl/job, poll to COMPLETED via delay_future
 - Retry on transport + retryable API status via delay_future, sharing the
   client's retry policy (max_attempts, retry_backoff, retry_statuses)
 - Async callbacks: external_callback strategy may return a plain hashref or a Future
 - deep_crawl: breadth-first crawl following each page's links, with each depth
   level's frontier crawled concurrently (concurrency knob); shares the link
   accessors and Result objects with WWW::Crawl4AI
 - Future-returning single-URL action endpoints mirroring WWW::Crawl4AI:
   screenshot / pdf (raw bytes), html, execute_js (page + js_result), llm, token
